00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.510
Ginko, and Onee-sama{さびしさと銀子とお姉さまの日}

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.620
What!? It’s already this late?!

00:02:55.620 --> 00:02:57.030
Onee-chan, wake up!

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.460
Wake up! We’re going to be late!

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:03.130
Just three more minutes…

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:09.580
This room is really dark, even in the morning.{T-3,2,1}

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.710
All because that high-rise got built next door.{TIME WARP TO A YEAR IN THE FUTURE (either that or the japanese are some of the damn fastest construction workers in the universe).}

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:20.170
The weather’s great today.{LOL THEY LIVE IN THE LUXURY MANSION COMPLEX}{wait didn’t they already have a fucking huge house?}

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:23.480
It looks like picking the penthouse was the right choice after all, Onee-sama.{Looks like picking the penthouse room was right, Onee-sama.}

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.830
You’d better hurry, Ginko. You’re going to be late.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:26.720
Yes, Onee-sama.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:31.530
I requested for father to build the apartments here so you would be closer to your school.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:32.400
O-Okay.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.830
You will not be allowed to be late.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:38.110
Y-Yes, Onee-sama.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:42.000
Even better, it’ll be much easier to find great sales from here!{And then we can go get our prize, the great deals!}

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:42.700
Right.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.310
<i>All we need are some pencils…{and now this line doesn’t really make sense. Oh well.}</i>

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:46.230
Nothing makes me happier than free things.

00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:47.660
<i>Weren’t they already cheap?</i>

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.310
“Economizing”. Oh, it sounds so marvelous.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:53.620
<i>I can’t handle much more of this.{Ginko is expressing her disapproval of her sister’s antics}</i>

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.250
Well then, I’ll be going ahead by car.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.220
I’ll be home late.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:02.800
H-H-Have a safe trip.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:08.530
<i>Onee-sama is busy today, too.</i>

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:12.230
Onee-chan, hurry up!

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:13.830
Okay!

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.440
If you don’t hurry, we’re going to be late!

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:25.150
Ah, it’s Ginko-chan!

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:26.870
Good morning!

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:27.530
Good morning!

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:29.990
Good morning.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:33.240
So you guys moved into the new apartment complex!{マンション (n) large apartment (from mansion); apartment house; FUCK YOU JAPAN}

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:35.280
Amazing, isn’t it?

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:37.460
Well, your old house was amazing too, of course.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.450
My father is the owner of these apartments.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:45.380
Because of that, we can live on whatever floor we want, but the penthouse is definitely the best one.

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:50.310
Maybe I’ll invite you over someday.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.610
Onee-chan, your scarf is a little crooked.

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.160
Thanks, Asu.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.770
Hey! Listen to me!

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.830
Ah, sorry.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.220
Um…

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.640
What were you talking about?

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:02.860
Onee-chan, we really need to…

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.550
Ah, that’s right.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:07.730
We’re going to be late, so let’s chat later.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:08.570
See you later!

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:10.280
Ah, me too!

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.630
<i>What the heck is it with those two?</i>

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.470
<i>Ah, I barely made it in time.</i>

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.930
<i>Could it be that the two of
them are always like that?</i>

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:36.890
Rise.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.160
Bow.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.810
<i>That’s just not the way things are between my sister and me.</i>

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.230
Good morning.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:41.820
Be seated.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:49.950
<i>Holding hands like that… how embarrassing.</i>

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:49.950
Class representative.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:51.740
Class representative!

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.050
Ah, yes?

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:56.790
What’s wrong? Come by the office later to pick up the printouts.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.460
Okay, I got it.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:00.420
Excuse me.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.620
You’re also a class representative?

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:08.290
Yeah.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:10.860
Everyone pushed the job on you, right?

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.870
I <i>had</i> to run for it.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.810
When I become a fifth grader, I’m going to run for the student council, too.

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:15.810
Ah, there you are!

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:17.890
I’ll definitely be elected president!

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:21.140
Asu-chan, can you please help me with the next part on this?

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:22.630
Oh, sure.

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:23.940
Hey! Listen to me!

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:25.790
Ah, sorry, Ginko-chan.

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:26.780
Please wait just a moment.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.930
It’s this part here.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:33.130
This part here helps to explain this other part here, which leads to—

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:35.360
Oh, I see! I get it now!

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:36.680
Asu-chan, you’re amazing!

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.560
Let me help you carry that.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.170
What up with her?

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:42.550
She’s just letting herself get used.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.470
Right?

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.020
You don’t seem busy.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.630
Help pass these out.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.070
Sorry, but we’re a little busy right now.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:54.700
Let’s go.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:55.350
Okay.

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.790
Echigoya-san is really annoying, don’t you think?{asdfj -> Echigoya}

00:06:58.790 --> 00:06:59.990
Yeah.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.650
Ginko-chan, sorry about what happened earlier.

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:14.770
Don’t follow me!

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:18.860
Didn’t I tell you to not follow me?!

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.070
We walk home the same way, though…

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:24.050
Asu-chan, are you heading home?

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.280
Good afternoon.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:28.270
You know, we made a little bit too much for today, so please take this home with you.

00:07:28.270 --> 00:07:29.930
Wow, it looks delicious!

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.660
Thank you very much!

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:32.440
You’re welcome.

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:32.910
Hey, Asu-chan!

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:34.940
These are today’s leftovers. Take them with you!

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:36.780
Ah, okay. Thank you.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.670
Asu-chan! I have some leftovers, too.

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:40.940
Ah. Okay!

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:43.710
Asu-chan, wait! You’d better take this too!

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:45.500
Okay. Thank you very much.

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:51.760
The way you and your sister get by on your own is really something.{You’re working so hard together with your sister, that’s amazing.}

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:53.630
It’s rare to see that these days.

00:07:53.630 --> 00:07:56.130
Here, this is from our store.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:57.740
Here. Extras, extras, take ’em.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.780
Oh, you’ve grown a bit taller, haven’t you?

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:02.370
<i>What do you mean it’s “really something”?</i>

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:06.780
<i>I’m also—I’m also trying my best with my older sister.{and an absurdly rich father who buys everything for them…}</i>

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.980
<i>Why is it? Why is it—?!</i>

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.050
I won’t lose to you!

00:08:14.330 --> 00:08:16.160
<i>I won’t lose to you two!</i>

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:25.020
<i>Why, why, why?!</i>

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:29.280
<i>Just because she’s nicer, has more
friends, and gets along with everyone!</i>

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:33.310
<i>Onee-sama and I are just so much, much, much—!{better implied by zutto?}</i>

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.280
Ginko.

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:38.120
Yes?

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:44.330
I had that long-range telescope that you asked for yesterday carried up from the ground floor.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:47.130
Thank you very much, Onee-sama.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:50.840
You asked for it so suddenly, I was wondering how on earth you were planning to use it.

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.920
You plan on doing some pretty risky things with it, right?{BORDERLINE ILLEGAL}

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:56.310
Ginko.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.220
You’re going to use this to…

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:03.240
Scout out all the supermarkets in the city for super-extraordinary sales, am I right?

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.350
That’s wonderful, Ginko.

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:06.940
Right, Onee-sama.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:10.650
If it’s for the great cause of economization, I’ll even lend you a helicopter if you want.

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:13.200
Onee-sama, I don’t think we need to go that far…

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.740
Whatever you’re doing, it’s a great idea.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:21.260
You should search every single supermarket for deals, even if it takes you the whole day.{Even if you have to spend the whole day, you have to find out every supermarket that has special sales.}

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.260
Sound good?

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:23.200
S-Sure.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.670
<i>I’m sorry, Onee-sama.</i>

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.350
<i>That’s not why I asked for the telescope.</i>

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:35.590
I have to go now, so I’ll leave the rest to you.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:38.870
What? You’re busy today too?

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:39.970
But we have the day off.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.310
Yes. I won’t be back until late tonight.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:45.470
Is that so?

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:46.930
Have a good day.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.610
Mistress, I’ve finished adjusting the settings.

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:54.050
I’ll take care of the rest.

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:54.910
Begone.{you may go}

00:09:54.910 --> 00:09:56.280
Understood.

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:04.950
<i>I’m aware that I really shouldn’t be doing this,</i>

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:10.500
<i>but I have to do it so I can find out just what it is that’s so different about them.</i>

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.410
<i>We should be perfect.</i>

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:15.630
<i>Even so, even so…</i>

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.450
<i>Yamada Asu!{YAMADA ASS}</i>

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:25.510
<i>I will definitely not lose to you!</i>

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:33.980
On a cold night, if you eat
shichimi, it will help keep you warm.

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:33.980
7 Delicious Spices{七味唐辛子 【しちみとうがらし】 (n) blend of seven spices (cayenne, sesame, Japanese pepper, citrus peel, etc.)}{七味唐がらし}

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:42.490
To us, the flea market is like
an enormous shopping mall.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.130
Thanks for the food!

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:10.630
<i>It’s delicious!</i>

00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:14.230
<i>The eggs and spinach is delicious!</i>

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:19.390
<i>Two days ago, I found the spinach on sale for 40 yen per bag.</i>

00:11:19.390 --> 00:11:23.160
<i>I cooked it with some eggs I found yesterday for 58 yen!</i>

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:26.870
Ah! The spinach from the sale that I missed!

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:38.810
<i>Why does she open her
mouth so wide while eating?</i>

00:11:38.810 --> 00:11:41.740
<i>Onee-sama would never do such an improper thing.</i>

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:46.220
<i>She even has grains of rice stuck to her face.</i>

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.500
<i>Why do they act so uncivilized?</i>

00:11:50.530 --> 00:11:53.480
Onee-chan, your face has some rice stuck to it, you know.

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:56.150
Oh my, you’re right.

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:02.610
<i>Ah, Onee-chan, the miso soup also came out really well today.</i>

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:08.860
I’ve never laughed during a meal before.

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:12.870
Talking with a full mouth is simply reprehensible behavior!{lol leaving it like this unless someone tells me to tone it down}

00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:18.380
What’s wrong, Asu?

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.100
Oh, it’s nothing.

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:42.050
<i>Today’s a holiday, so she’s sleeping on the floor in the middle of the day?{休み [やすみ] 1: rest; recess; respite; 2: vacation; holiday; absence; suspension;}</i>

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:45.320
<i>I’ve never seen Onee-sama being that lazy.</i>

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:49.060
<i>Even until she goes to bed, she’s always energetic and—</i>

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:51.200
Ginko, good night.

00:12:51.980 --> 00:12:55.270
<i>Onee-sama, perhaps you’re a little too energetic.</i>

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:05.500
<i>Why does she always seem so happy to take care of her troublesome older sister?</i>

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:11.350
<i>It’s rough, isn’t it, Yamada Asu.{flat what}</i>

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:17.970
<i>My sister is never troublesome or dependent on me.</i>

00:13:23.420 --> 00:13:25.990
Ah, Kyou-chan, Asu-chan, good afternoon.

00:13:25.990 --> 00:13:26.780
Good afternoon!

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.980
What’s this, the two of you are out for a walk?

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:29.790
Yeah.

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:31.630
You two sure seem to get along well.

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:33.450
You’re nothing like my kids.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.960
They’re always fighting with each other.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:39.420
<i>They could learn a thing or two from you guys.{wait, so she has the microphones on asu and kyou? and what’s their workable range?}</i>

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.760
<i>No way, you’re flattering us, ma’am.</i>

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:45.660
Ta-da!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.930
Asu, go ahead and pick whichever one you like.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.460
I’ll take this one—the dried tuna!

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:52.310
I’ll go with the picked plum, then.

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.590
<i>Let’s eat!</i>

00:13:57.090 --> 00:14:00.480
Asu, this pickled plum rice ball is really good!

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:03.570
All they ever think about is food, huh?

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:07.200
All rice balls taste the same no matter who makes them.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.810
There’s absolutely no reason for me to be jealous of them.

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.790
<i>Asu-chan, you’re early today, aren’t you?</i>

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:17.240
Good afternoon!

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:19.180
Thank you for yesterday.

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:21.250
We have the day off today, so I came together with my sister!

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:24.620
<i>Mister, do you have anything that’s especially cheap today?{Mister, are there any cheap fish?}</i>

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:28.220
<i>Those two have been together since they woke up.</i>

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:33.190
Mistress Ginko, don’t you think that spying on people is a little…

00:14:34.110 --> 00:14:35.390
I’m through with it.

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:39.230
Watching any more would be a waste of time.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:43.520
What’s wrong, Asu?

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.910
For some reason I’ve been on edge today.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.910
It kind of feels like someone is watching us.

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:54.280
That’s kinda odd, Asu.{silly?}

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:59.080
Hey, isn’t it time for you to deliver the newspaper?

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:01.590
Ah, this is bad! Today’s the evening edition, isn’t it?

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:03.390
Sorry, can you take these home?

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:05.110
They’re a little heavy. See ya!

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:06.000
Take care!

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.300
I’m home!

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:10.830
Onee-chan, welcome home.

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:12.420
Dinner is ready.

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:14.430
Ah, thank you.

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:19.480
Mistress Ginko, we’ve completed the dinner preparations.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:20.680
Just leave it there.

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:21.430
Very well.{LULZ, "very well"?}

00:15:22.670 --> 00:15:23.560
Wait.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.000
Yes, is there something you need?

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.130
Father hasn’t come home yet?

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:31.820
Your father has not yet returned from his trip to Los Angeles.

00:15:32.120 --> 00:15:33.360
And your mother—

00:15:33.360 --> 00:15:34.330
That’s enough.

00:15:35.670 --> 00:15:38.160
That’s enough. You’re dismissed.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:42.180
Thanks for the food!

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:47.570
Asu! This Salmon Meunière is the best!{I shit you not they’re eating french food (capitalized and accented for full irony). ムニエル (n) meuniere (fre:) -> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meuniere_sauce}

00:15:47.570 --> 00:15:50.550
The man from the fish market was nice enough to sell us this salmon at a really low price,

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:53.140
and the side dishes are from the owner of the vegetable stand.

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:57.130
“Meunier” certainly has a rich sound to it.

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:59.600
Even though I only sprinkled a few croûtons on top.{more accents for frenchie lulz}

00:16:13.350 --> 00:16:14.410
<i>I’m all right.{HOT GINKO BATHTUB SCENE UNF}</i>

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:23.290
<i>I’m fine with being alone.</i>

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:28.400
<i>I </i>was<i> fine, but…</i>

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.930
<i>But still, why?</i>

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.350
<i>Why am I still drawn to the light from that window?</i>

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:46.440
Come over to my house.

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:47.380
Wha—?{I am Kyou, this is my derpface: "HURR DURR DERP A HERPDERP"}

00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.790
I told you before that I’d invite you over!

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:53.820
But it’s already so late, and shouldn’t you ask your family for permission firs—

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:55.860
There’s nobody there to ask!

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:03.000
Wow! It’s so beautiful!

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:06.290
Yeah, isn’t it amazing?

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:09.610
The building over there, the tallest one, is ours too.

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:11.480
Along with that one, and that one.

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:12.760
In this area we own a bunch—

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.600
No, no, Onee-chan! We’re in someone else’s house!

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:17.830
You can’t fall asleep here!

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:23.040
I’m sorry, it’s just that she’s usually asleep by this time.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:23.770
Onee-cha—!

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:26.770
Ah, she really fell asleep.

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.180
She’s not a very reliable older sister, is she?

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:32.640
That’s why you’re always working so hard.

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:33.690
It’s tough, isn’t it.

00:17:36.280 --> 00:17:37.660
It’s not tough at all.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:40.120
It’s okay. Don’t lie.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:45.330
If it’s for Onee-chan, I’ll do my very best.

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:49.770
Every day, she attends school and works as well.

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.750
She’s really the one who has it rough.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.200
Onee-sama…

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:12.440
Because I can’t get a real job yet,

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:16.950
for Onee-chan’s sake,

00:18:17.370 --> 00:18:22.410
I want to make our home the one place in the world where she doesn’t have to work hard.

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:31.680
A place where she doesn’t have to work hard…

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:32.300
Yes.

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:36.340
Asu, this fried sweet potato is also really delicious.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:39.190
Well then, we’ll head home now.

00:18:39.190 --> 00:18:39.940
Okay.

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:41.480
Onee-chan, it’s time to go.

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:43.710
Yes… It’s delicious.

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:44.350
Geez…{JESUS H CHRIST}

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:48.030
<i>What can I do for my sister?</i>

00:18:48.510 --> 00:18:50.980
Excuse me…

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.980
Excuse us!

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:56.460
<i>Onee-sama always does her best to meet the expectations of those around her,</i>

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:59.400
<i>and I’ve never heard her once complain about how tough it is.</i>

00:19:01.170 --> 00:19:04.400
<i>Onee-sama is the one who is always alone.</i>

00:19:07.390 --> 00:19:11.670
<i>No, I was the one who abandoned her.</i>

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:22.340
Mistress Kinko, will it be satisfactory to leave Mistress Ginko’s new clothes here?{argh verb tenses and general phraseology}

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:25.180
Sure. Just leave them on the table.

00:19:25.180 --> 00:19:26.240
But…

00:19:26.240 --> 00:19:28.520
It’s fine. I’ll take care of them.

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:29.940
Understood.

00:19:29.940 --> 00:19:31.620
Well then, I’ll retire for today.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:32.700
Thank you.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:34.910
Onee-sa—

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:46.060
Onee-sama.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:50.670
You’re not asleep yet?

00:19:50.670 --> 00:19:51.510
No.

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:55.170
You should hurry to bed, Ginko. You have school tomorrow.

00:19:55.990 --> 00:19:57.340
What about you, Onee-sama?

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:00.650
There are still some things that I have to take care of.

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:08.140
My laundry—you’re the one who always folds it for me, aren’t you?

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.350
Onee-sama!

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:22.780
Onee-sama, please don’t push yourself too hard!

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:27.690
Ginko.{GODDAMN FUCKING LASER EYES}

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:34.600
I understand.

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:40.960
Thank you, Ginko.

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:48.820
<i>Dear Onee-sama,</i>

00:20:48.820 --> 00:20:52.350
<i>today I noticed something for the first time.</i>

00:20:52.430 --> 00:20:55.240
<i>I was the one who was wrong.</i>

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:58.330
<i>I was always thinking only about myself.</i>

00:20:58.890 --> 00:21:04.150
<i>I didn’t even notice how much you have been taking care of me all this time.</i>

00:21:04.640 --> 00:21:06.250
<i>I finally understand.</i>

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:11.250
<i>The most precious feelings are those that two people share for each other.</i>

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:14.620
<i>That’s why I love you, Onee-sama.{THIS IS MY THESIS, MY MASTERWORK}</i>

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:21.620
I should be able to create it.

00:21:22.110 --> 00:21:24.110
A place where she doesn’t have to work hard.

